$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of (3S, 4R)-(-)-4-Phenyl-3-carbethoxy-2-pyrrolidinone 9: The
mixture of 6a (93% ee, 0.1 mmol, 27.5 mg), ethyl acetate (1 mL), acetic
acid (50 uL), 10% Pd/C (12 mg) or Raney-nickel (ca. 62.5 mg, 0.1mL
suspension in EtOH; Note: after the reaction of Ni-Al with NaOH(aq.), the
catalyst was washed with water untill pH value was detected to be below
9.0) was stirred under 2 MPa of hydrogen at 55°C. After 18 h, catalyst
was filtered off under reduced pressure and the solid was washed with
ethyl acetate (2 mL×3). After evaporating the solvent, the residue was
subjected to silica gel column chromatography (ether/ethyl acetate, 1/1,
V/V) to afford the desired product 9 as an oil (18 mg, 76 % yield, 93%
ee). (3S, 4R)-(-)-4-Phenyl-3-carbethoxy-2-pyrrolidinone 9, (18 mg, 76 %
yield, 93% ee) [α]D 21 = -89.6 (c = 0.634 in CHCl3). HPLC (DAICEL
CHIRALCEL OD-H, 2-propanol/n-hexane = 20/80, flow rate = 1.0 mL/min, λ=
210 nm, retention time: 12.0 min (major) and 14.2 min (minor); 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 1.28 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 3.44 (t, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H),
3.56 (d, J = 9.6 Hz, 1H), 3.84 (t, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 4.12 (q, J = 8.8 Hz,
1H), 4.26 (q, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 6.39 (br s, 1H), 7.23-7.38 (m, 5H) ppm;
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 172.2, 169.2, 139.9, 129.0, 127.6, 127.0,
61.8, 55.0, 47.5, 44.4, 14.1 ppm. (Raney-nickel reduction of 6a is a
modified method according to Ref. 4.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternatively raney-nickel was used as catalyst, ee=93%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Cyanation of Activated Olefins with Ethyl Cyanoformate
Catalyzed by a Modular Titanium Catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Jun; Li, Wei; Liu, Yanling; Chu, Yangyang; Lin, Lili; Liu, Xiaohua;
Feng, Xiaoming
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(6), 1280-1283

