$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Reduction of β-Amino
Nitriles 5 to Monoprotected 1,3-Diamino Derivatives 6. To a stirred
suspension of LiAlH4 (6.5 mmol) in diethyl ether (7 mL) was added
dropwise a solution of AlCl3 (6.68 mmol) in diethyl ether (7 mL) at room
temperature. β-Amino nitrile 5 (2.5 mmol) dissolved in diethyl ether (7
mL) was then added, and stirring was continued for an additional 4 h. The
mixture was cooled in an ice bath and treated with 3 N NaOH (8 mL), and
the aqueous phase was separated and extracted with diethyl ether (4 ×
15mL). The organic phase was washed with brine and dried over MgSO4; the
crude product was obtained after evaporation if the solvent at reduced
pressure was purified by column chromatography (92:8:0.1
dichloromethane-methanol-38% NH4OH). tert-Butyl
3-Amino-1,2-diphenylpropyl Carbamate (6k). Yield: 75%, oil. IR (cm-1,
neat): 3300. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) syn δ: 1.32 (s, 9H), 1.79 (bs, 2H),
2.78-3.10 (m, 3H), 4.84-5.15 (m, 2H), 7.05-7.38 (m, 10H); anti δ: 1.43
(s, 9H), 1.65 (bs, 2H), 3.05-3.32 (m, 3H), 5.66-5.80 (m, 2H), 7.05-7.40
(m, 10H). Anal. Calcd for C20H26N2O2 (326.44): C, 73.59; H, 8.03; N,
8.58. Found: C, 73.51; H, 7.95; N, 8.63.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in-situ generated reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reaction of α-Amidoalkylphenyl Sulfones with Lithiated Nitriles:
Syn-Selective Synthesis of β-Amino Nitriles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mecozzi, Tiziana; Petrini, Marino; Profeta, Roberto
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2001), 66(24), 8264-8267

