$DATUM 6-Amino-5-hydroxy-5-morpholin-4-yl-2,3,5,6-tetrahydro-1H-pyrrolizine-7-carbonitrile
7 Compound 8 (1 g, 7.5 mmol) was dissolved in morpholine (5 ml), then
formaldehyde solution (34%) (0.75 ml, 7.5 mmol) was added portion wise.
The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature for 24 h, poured
over cooled water and left overnight in a refrigerator. The formed
crystals were filtered, washed with water and crystallized from ethanol.
Yield 75%. m.p. 150-152°C, IR: νmax/cm-1 3477 (OH), 3410, 3289 (NH2),
2956, 2845 (CH aliphatic), 2197 (CN), 1632, 1586 (NH, C=C), 1482, 1312
(C-N, C-O). 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3: δ, ppm): 2.09-2.15 (m, 2H, CH2-2),
2.53-2.56 (m, 4H, N(CH2)2), 2.90 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H, CH2-1), 3.64-3.71
(m, 6H, O(CH2)2, CH2-3), 4.10 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H, CH-6), 6.14 (s, 2H, NH2
exchangeable with D2O), 9.51 (s, 1H, OH) exchangeable with D2O. 13C NMR
(DMSO-d6): d 20.22 (C-2), 33.42 (C-1), 49.03 (C-3), 49.97 (N(CH2)), 51.55
(C-7), 60.06 (C-6), 66.12 (O(CH2)),120.07 (CN), 167.02 (C-5), 171.55
(C-7a). MS: m/z (%) 250 (M , 5), 100 (100). Anal. Calcd. for C12H18N4O2
(250.30): C, 57.58, H, 7.25, N, 22.38. Found: C, 57.81, H, 6.87, N,
21.97.
