$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the one-pot preparation of δ-amino alcohols (9a,
9b, 9c, 9e) :(S)-4-amino-4-phenylbutan-1-ol : To a solution of
benzonitrile (300mg, 2.9 mmol) in diethyl ether (5 ml) lithium
triethylborohydride (2;1 M in THF; 2.9 mL, 2.9 mmol) was added at 0 °C
and the solution was stirred for 2h.Methanol (92 mg, 2.9 mmol) was added
to the reaction mixture and stirred for 30minutes. The reaction mixture
was cooled to -100 °C and slowly transferred to via canulato a stirring
solution of (-)-B-allyldiisopinocampheylborane (5, 1 M in diethyl ether;
3.48mL, 3.48 mmol) pre-cooled to -100 °C and diluted with ether. After 6
h, the reactionmixture was slowly warmed to -78 °C and stirring was
continued for 16 h more. 10 MBH3-SMe2 (0.435 mL, 4.35 mmol) in 3 mL Et2O
was added to the reaction mixture andstirred for 48 h while slowly
warming to room temperature. Then the reaction mixturewas oxidised very
slowly with NaOH (3 M in H2O; 2.8 mL) and H2O2 (30% in H2O; 2.8mL) and
was left stirring overnight under positive N2 pressure. The product was
thenextracted with Et2O (3X30 mL), the combined organic layer was washed
with saturatedbrine solution and dried over anhy. Na2SO4. Next, the
solvent was evaporated underreduced pressure, and the material was
purified on silica gel (dichloromethane : methanol: triethylamine 94.5 :
4.5 : 0.5) to afford product. Yield 359 mg 2.18 mmol, 75%. 1HNMR: (300
MHz, CDCl3)δ 7.34-7.20 (m, 5H), 3.86 (dd, J=7.3 Hz, J=5.4 Hz, 1H),
3.67-3.51 (m, 2H), 2.95 (br s, 2H), 1.86-1.69 (m, 2H), 1.65-1.57 (m, 2H);
13C NMR: (75 MHz,CDCl3)δ 146.4, 128.6, 127.1, 126.0, 62.6, 56.2, 37.1,
30.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
