$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Reduction of β-Amino Nitriles 5 to
Monoprotected 1,3-Diamino Derivatives 6. To a stirred suspension of
LiAlH4 (6.5 mmol) in diethyl ether (7 mL) was added dropwise a solution
of AlCl3 (6.68 mmol) in diethyl ether (7 mL) at room temperature. β-Amino
nitrile 5 (2.5 mmol) dissolved in diethyl ether (7 mL) was then added,
and stirring was continued for an additional 4 h. The mixture was cooled
in an ice bath and treated with 3 N NaOH (8 mL), and the aqueous phase
was separated and extracted with diethyl ether (4 × 15mL). The organic
phase was washed with brine and dried over MgSO4; the crude product was
obtained after evaporation if the solvent at reduced pressure was
purified by column chromatography (92:8:0.1 dichloromethane-methanol-38%
NH4OH). tert-Butyl 1-(2-Amino-1-phenylethyl)-3-methylbutyl Carbamate
(6j). Yield: 73%, oil. IR (cm-1, neat): 3300. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) syn
δ: 0.83 (d, 3H, J = 6.7 Hz), 0.87 (d, 3H, J = 6.7 Hz), 0.95-1.05 (m, 1H),
1.08-1.18 (m, 1H), 1.41 (s, 9H), 1.52-1.68 (m, 1H), 2.69 (dt, 1H, J =
2.8, 7.1 Hz), 2.91 (dd, 1H, J = 7.1, 12.8 Hz), 3.06 (dd, 1H, J = 8.2,
12.8 Hz), 4.05-4.10 (m, 1H), 4.30 (d, 1H, J = 10.2 Hz), 7.12-7.38 (m,
5H); anti δ: 0.76 (d, 3H, J = 6.7 Hz), 0.86 (d, 3H, J = 6.7 Hz),
0.95-1.05 (m, 1H), 1.08-1.18 (m, 1H), 1.43 (s, 9H), 1.52-1.68 (m, 1H),
2.56 (dt, 1H, J = 4.9, 8.5 Hz), 2.97-3.04 (m, 2H), 3.88-3.97 (m, 1H),
4.09 (d, 1H, J = 9.5 Hz), 7.12-7.38 (m, 5H). Anal. Calcd for C18H30N2O2
(306.45): C, 70.55; H, 9.87; N, 9.14. Found: C, 70.49; H, 9.90; N, 9.11.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
