$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the one-pot preparation
of δ-amino alcohols (9a, 9b, 9c, 9e) :(S)-4-amino-4-phenylbutan-1-ol : To
a solution of benzonitrile (300mg, 2.9 mmol) in diethyl ether (5 ml)
lithium triethylborohydride (2;1 M in THF; 2.9 mL, 2.9 mmol) was added at
0 °C and the solution was stirred for 2h.Methanol (92 mg, 2.9 mmol) was
added to the reaction mixture and stirred for 30minutes. The reaction
mixture was cooled to -100 °C and slowly transferred to via canulato a
stirring solution of (-)-B-allyldiisopinocampheylborane (5, 1 M in
diethyl ether; 3.48mL, 3.48 mmol) pre-cooled to -100 °C and diluted with
ether. After 6 h, the reactionmixture was slowly warmed to -78 °C and
stirring was continued for 16 h more. 10 MBH3-SMe2 (0.435 mL, 4.35 mmol)
in 3 mL Et2O was added to the reaction mixture andstirred for 48 h while
slowly warming to room temperature. Then the reaction mixturewas oxidised
very slowly with NaOH (3 M in H2O; 2.8 mL) and H2O2 (30% in H2O; 2.8mL)
and was left stirring overnight under positive N2 pressure. The product
was thenextracted with Et2O (3X30 mL), the combined organic layer was
washed with saturatedbrine solution and dried over anhy. Na2SO4. Next,
the solvent was evaporated underreduced pressure, and the material was
purified on silica gel (dichloromethane : methanol: triethylamine 94.5 :
4.5 : 0.5) to afford product. (S)-4-amino-4-(4-methoxyphenyl)butan-1-ol.
Yield 71%. 1H NMR: (300 MHz, CDCl3)δ 7.20-7.14 (m, 2H), 6.85-6.79 (m,
2H), 3.84-3.76 (m, 4H),3.60-3.53 (m, 2H), 3.18 (br s, 2H), 1.77-1.69 (m,
2H), 1.60-1.51 (m, 2H); 13C NMR: (75MHz, CDCl3)δ 158.6, 138.3, 127.1,
113.9, 62.5, 55.3, 55.2, 36.9, 30.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
