$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure C: Starting material (100
mg, nitroaryl or nitroalkyl) was dissolved in MeOH and stirred at room
temperature. 5 % Pd/C (0.039 g, 1.8 x 10-5 mol) and NH4HCO2 (0.60 g, 9.5
x 10-3 mol) dissolved in H2O (1.0 mL) was then added to the reaction
mixture while stirring. The reaction was monitored by TLC or GCMS (for
nitroalkyl) for the in situ reduction of nitro compound to the
corresponding primary amine. Nitrile (8 eq) was then added to the
reaction mixture and stirring was continued until the primary amine
intermediate (lowest Rf) was no longer detected by TLC. The reaction
mixture was filtered, washed successively with methanol and CH2Cl2 and
the filtrate evaporated in vacuo. The residue was dissolved in CH2Cl2 and
the organic layer was separated, dried in Na2SO4 and filtered. The
filtrate was then evaporated in vacuo to give the product. Starting from
nitrobenzene (0.10 g, 8.1 x 10-4 mol), MeOH (3.4 mL), butyronitrile (0.57
mL, 6.6 x 10-3 mol) using general procedure C gave a light brown liquid
(0.085 g, 71 %). Rf 0.58 (10:1 hexanes:ethyl acetate); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3, δH) 0.99 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 1.41-1.50 (m, 2H), 1.59-1.67 (m,
2H), 3.13 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 6.63 (m, 2H), 6.71 (m, 1H), 7.20 (m, 2H);
13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, δC) 14.1, 20.6, 32.0, 43.9, 113.0, 117.3, 129.
5, 148.8; GCMS (EI) m/z 149.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reductive monoalkylation of aromatic and aliphatic nitro compounds and
the corresponding amines with nitriles
