$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: MCR of aldehydes, 2-naphthol, and
nitriles/amides utilizing SiCl4/ZnCl2; General procedure: To a solution
of anhydrous ZnCl2 (0.7 g, 5 mmol) in ClCH2CH2Cl (or DCM) (20 ml) were
added aldehyde (5 mmol), 2-naphthol (5 mmol), and nitrile/amide (6.5
mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 10 min
SiCl4 (1.2 ml, 10 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was stirred
with exclusion of moisture. On completion (TLC monitoring of the progress
of the reaction), the mixture was poured onto aq. Na2CO3 (100 ml),
extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 × 50 ml) and the combined organic extract dried
over anhydrous MgSO4, evaporated and the residue chromatographed on
silica gel using pet. ether-ethyl acetate (1:1 for 4,5,6e,f and 2:1 for
7-10) as eluent. 1-amidoalkyl naphthol 8a, Yield: 70%. Time: 18 h.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, Ritter-type reaction, alternative preparation shown,
alternate solvent (dichloromethane) may be used in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Silicon-induced general, mild, and efficient one-pot, three-component
synthesis of amidoalkyl naphthol libraries
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Salama, Tarek A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2013), 24(6), 713-718

