$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 6-Trifluoromethylindole (4). Five percent palladium on
charcoal catalyst paste (6.18 kg containing 52.8% water, 2.92 kg) and
benzyl 2-cyano-2-(2-nitro-4-trifluoromethylphenyl)ethanoate (26.78 kg @
77.5%, 57.0 mol) were charged to a hydrogenation vessel. Ethanol (159 L),
glacial acetic acid (16 L), and water (15 L) were added and the reaction
mixture stirred vigorously under an atmosphere of hydrogen at 26-42 psig
between 19-36°C for 23 h. The catalyst was removed by filtration through
Celite (2 kg) and the filter bed washed with ethanol (50 L). The combined
filtrate was concentrated in vacuo at 22-33°C over 2 h to a volume of 165
L and water (330 L) was added over 20 min. The suspension was stirred at
20°C for 30 min and the product collected by filtration. The product was
washed with water (40 L) and then dried under vacuum to give 8.36 kg
(79%) yield. 6-Trifluoromethylindole (4), yield 8.36 kg, 79%. 4: M.p.
111-113°C (aq. IMS), (Lit.[4] m.p. 109-110°C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
8.20 (1H, br s, N-H), {[7.70 (1H, d, J 8.4), 7.61 (1H, s), 7.35 (1H, d, J
8.7), 7.38 (1H, app t, J 2.8), 6.56-6.61 (1H, m)], Ar-H}. 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3): δ 134.6, 130.2, 126.8, 128.4, (q, J 271.7), 124.5 (q, J
31.3), 121.1, 116.5 (q, J 4.0), 108.6 (q, J 4.0), 102.9. m/z (EIMS)
Found: M+ 185.0453. C9H6F3N requires M, 185.0452.
