$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of 6-Trifluoromethylindole (4).
Five percent palladium on charcoal catalyst paste (6.18 kg containing
52.8% water, 2.92 kg) and benzyl
2-cyano-2-(2-nitro-4-trifluoromethylphenyl)ethanoate (26.78 kg @ 77.5%,
57.0 mol) were charged to a hydrogenation vessel. Ethanol (159 L),
glacial acetic acid (16 L), and water (15 L) were added and the reaction
mixture stirred vigorously under an atmosphere of hydrogen at 26-42 psig
between 19-36°C for 23 h. The catalyst was removed by filtration through
Celite (2 kg) and the filter bed washed with ethanol (50 L). The combined
filtrate was concentrated in vacuo at 22-33°C over 2 h to a volume of 165
L and water (330 L) was added over 20 min. The suspension was stirred at
20°C for 30 min and the product collected by filtration. The product was
washed with water (40 L) and then dried under vacuum to give 8.36 kg
(79%) yield. Table 1. Entry: 2, yield 88%.
