$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a mixture of nitrile (1 mmol) and EtOH-H2O
(1:1, 5mL), sodium borohydride (0.75 equiv) was added. The reaction
solution was stirred at 80°C, and the progress of the reaction was
monitored by thin-layer chromatography (TLC) (silica gel; hexane/ ethyl
acetate) and GC-MS. After completion, the reaction mixture was diluted
with MeOH to dissolve all the precipitate. The entire mixture was
transferred into a 50-mL round-bottom flask, evaporated in vacuo, and
concentrated. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica
gel (hexane-ethyl acetate). Amide. Entry: 11 Product: B, Yield: 87%
Product: C, Yield: 13%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM agent concentration dependent product formation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Transition metal-free sodium borohydride-promoted controlled hydration of
nitriles to amides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
